description:
Design a 3-bit up-counter with asynchronous reset functionality. The counter increments its value on each rising edge of the clock signal. When the counter reaches a maximum value of 7 (binary 111), it wraps around to 0. The counter can be reset to 0 immediately when the reset signal is activated. This design incorporates two pipeline stages to hold the count values, ensuring stability in counting operations.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input rst,
    output reg [2:0] count
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input rst,
    output reg [2:0] count
);reg [2:0] count_reg1, count_reg2;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    count_reg1 <= count;
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
    count_reg2 <= count_reg1;
end

always @(*) begin
    if (rst) begin
        count <= 3'b0;
    end else if (count_reg2 == 3'b111) begin
        count <= 3'b0;
    end else begin
        count <= count_reg2 + 1;
    end
end

endmodule

