description:
Design a 4-bit synchronous register with an active-low reset feature. On the rising edge of the clock, if the reset signal (rst_l) is low, the output (q) is set to zero. Otherwise, the output is updated to the value presented at the input (d). This module is useful for storing 4 bits of data in a timing-sensitive application where reset functionality is needed.
module top_module(/*AUTOARG*/
   // Outputs
   q,
   // Inputs
   clk, rst_l, d
   );

code:
module top_module(/*AUTOARG*/
   // Outputs
   q,
   // Inputs
   clk, rst_l, d
   );input clk;
   input rst_l;
   input [3:0] d;
   output reg [3:0] q;

   always @(posedge clk, negedge rst_l) begin
      if (~rst_l) begin
         q <= 4'b0000;
      end else begin
         q <= d;
      end
   end

endmodule

