description:
Design a standard SR latch using the inputs 's' (set) and 'r' (reset) to control the output states 'q' and 'qbar'. When 's' is activated (1) and 'r' is deactivated (0), the latch sets 'q' to 1 and 'qbar' to 0. When 'r' is activated and 's' is deactivated, it resets 'q' to 0 and 'qbar' to 1. If both inputs are activated simultaneously, the outputs are set to an indeterminate state (both outputs as 0), while a default case handles any undefined input conditions.
module top_module(
    input s, r,
    output reg q, qbar
);

code:
module top_module(
    input s, r,
    output reg q, qbar
);always @ (*)
        case({s, r})
            2'b01: {q, qbar} = 2'b01;
            2'b10: {q, qbar} = 2'b10;
            2'b11: {q, qbar} = 2'b00;
            default: {q, qbar} = 2'bxx;
        endcase
endmodule

